    "verdict": "ARGUS LOSES to every published baseline on sentiment classification. Its crowd read now scores tone with VADER on every post the abuse screen keeps: macro-recall 0.544 (95% CI 0.535-0.553), up from the 0.333 floor it scored with no polarity. VADER alone scores 0.570, finBERT (the capability's named baseline) 0.396, the paper's weakest baseline BLSTM 0.583 and the best reported model TimeLMs-2021 (README leaderboard) 0.737. Against VADER alone it is -0.026 (paired 95% CI -0.030 to -0.023): that is the abuse screen's cost, since a withheld post gets no tone. Against finBERT it is +0.148 (+0.138 to +0.159). RoB-RT, re-scored here at 0.729, is still 0.185 ahead: a tweet-domain transformer closes that at the cost of torch in the runtime. ARGUS's LLM analyst was not run (Qwen budget zero).",
