    "tone_bias_from_the_abuse_screen": "The abuse screen lowers the negative share a reader is shown: per 60-post sweep, screened minus unscreened is -1.51% (95% CI -1.74% to -1.30%, 205 sweeps). Gold negative share is 32.3% of all tweets and 30.0% of the ones kept. Against the gold share of the whole sweep, VADER's negative share is -2.51% unscreened and -4.02% screened, so the screen adds to a bias VADER already has. The withheld tweets, had they been scored, would have read {'positive': 180, 'neutral': 101, 'negative': 375}. The coordination weighting moved the negative share by +0.01% on this organic benchmark (1 coordinated stories formed in all sweeps), as expected where nobody is brigading."
