    "verdict": "Before the screen, social_pulse counted every abusive post and quoted 63 coordinated abusive HatEval lines back to the reader in the brigade scenario; with it, 0. The screen withholds 61.4% of hateful and 40.4% of offensive test posts, and 5.6% of clean ones. Macro-F1 0.524 on hate and 0.695 on offensive: a word screen, so hostility with no listed word in it passes and is still counted. Brigade quotes fall to zero because the console no longer quotes any coordinated story's text (the screen alone left every sweep quoting a missed line); in the organic scenario 1 missed abusive line(s) were still quoted as the most-shared story. TweetEval's RoB-RT, re-scored on the same items, reaches 0.555 and 0.816: the regression check still finds a defect \u2014 abusive posts the screen misses are counted as crowd volume \u2014 and what would close it is a trained classifier, which the runtime's no-torch rule currently excludes."
